<name>Starting</name>
<ttl id="10024_S000T_744HN_T007Z" variety="T007Z">
<name>Smart Entry &amp; Start System (Start System)</name>
<para id="X39400000I600RC" category="C" type-id="304MU" name-id="161X4-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>B2271</dtccode>
<dtcname>IG Circuit Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="X39400000I600RC_10" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000049200000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>This DTC is output when a malfunction such as an open or short in the IG output circuit inside the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU) is detected.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When using the TaSCAN with the IG OFF, repeatedly turn any door courtesy light switch ON and OFF (at intervals of 1.5 seconds or less) until communication between the TaSCAN and the vehicle starts.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>The Smart Entry &amp; Start System (start system) has functions that use multiplex communication. First, follow "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting" and confirm that there is no malfunction in the communication system before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>When the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU) is replaced with a new ECU and the battery negative terminal is connected, it enters the IG ON state. Also, when the battery is removed and reinstalled, the power source returns to the state it was in when the battery was removed.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1" pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<colspec colnum="01" colname="C01" colwidth="1.01in"/>
<colspec colnum="02" colname="C02" colwidth="2.30in"/>
<colspec colnum="03" colname="C03" colwidth="3.77in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B2271</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="left">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Malfunction in the IG1/IG2 output circuit inside the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" valign="middle" align="left">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Instrument Panel J/B Assembly (Main Body ECU)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>AM2 NO.2 7.5A fuse</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Wire Harness or Connector</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="X39400000I600RC_11" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000049300000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A161585J01" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="X39400000I600RC_12" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="X39400000I600RC_13" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="X39400000I600RC_13_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___000049400000">
<testtitle>Check DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Clear the DTCs, check the DTCs again, and check that no DTC is output.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.30in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.83in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC is output again</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>No DTC is output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000I600RC_13_0005" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="X39400000I600RC_13_0003" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000I600RC_13_0005" proc-id="RM0550J___000049500000">
<testtitle>Inspect Fuse</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance of the fuse.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.67in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.09in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>AM2 NO.2 fuse</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000I600RC_13_0006" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="X39400000I600RC_13_0004" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000I600RC_13_0006" proc-id="RM0550J___000049600000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness (Power Source)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Voltage Inspection</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A161604J01" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<test2>
<ptxt>Disconnect connectors U and V of the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU).</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), inspect the voltage between each terminal of the vehicle side wire harness connector and body ground.</ptxt>
</test2>
</test1>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.25in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL4" colwidth="0.88in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>U1 (AM1) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>11 to 14V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>V6 (AM2) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>11 to 14V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000I600RC_13_0002" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="X39400000I600RC_13_0007" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000I600RC_13_0002">
<testtitle>Replace instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU)</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000I600RC_13_0003">
<testtitle>END</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000I600RC_13_0004">
